Article 1 These Provisions apply to the following disputes arising when a freight forwarding enterprise accepts the entrustment of a principal and handles freight forwarding affairs related to maritime carriage of goods:
(1) disputes arising from the provision of booking, customs declaration, inspection declaration, commodity inspection declaration, and insurance services;
(2) disputes arising from the provision of services such as packing, loading supervision, unloading supervision, container stuffing and stripping, distribution, and transshipment of goods;
(3) disputes arising from the preparation and delivery of relevant documents and fee settlement;
(4) disputes arising from the provision of warehousing and road transportation services;
(5) disputes arising from the handling of other maritime freight forwarding affairs.
